# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context for the decode server (MVP W9).
#
# ⚠ TWO TRAPS LIVE HERE, and both were hit before the first real deploy.
#
# 1. **The weights are gitignored.** Without this file, gcloud derives the upload list from
#    `.gitignore` — and `apps/web/public/models/` is excluded there because the graphs are too big
#    for GitHub. The build would arrive with no model in it.
#
# 2. **A bare `src/` or `tools/` matches at EVERY depth**, not just the root — that is gitignore
#    syntax, and it is what these patterns are. Written unanchored, `src/` silently excluded
#    `apps/web/src/`, which holds `omr/decode.ts`, the one module the whole server design exists to
#    reuse; and `tools/` excluded `apps/server/tools/prepare-models.mjs`, which the Dockerfile runs
#    to assemble the model directory. **Every root-only exclusion below is anchored with a leading
#    slash for this reason. Do not remove the slashes.**
#
# The Dockerfile copies: package manifests, packages/core, apps/server, apps/web/src and
# apps/web/public/models. Everything else is excluded, because `data/` alone is tens of gigabytes.

.git/
.gitignore
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Training and research material — none of it ships (CLAUDE.md: Python is training/data only).
/data/
/.venv-ml/
/src/
/scripts/
/docs/
/archive/
/tools/

# Build outputs and local state.
/dist/
/apps/web/dist/
/apps/server/dist/
/apps/server/models/
*.log

# Browser-only assets: the server never serves a page. `ort/` is 26 MB of wasm for the web build,
# `scores/` ~20 MB of render-automation corpus, `probe/` the opencv reference dumps.
/apps/web/public/ort/
/apps/web/public/scores/
/apps/web/public/probe/
/apps/web/public/fonts/

# The gate's 14 test strips sit beside the graphs; `prepare-models.mjs` reads gate.json for the
# token map and drops the fixture, so the images themselves never need to travel.
/apps/web/public/models/*.png
/apps/web/public/models/*.pixels.bin
